WEBVTT

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.110
Look at this!

00:00:08.110 --> 00:00:10.600
I bought a new bathing suit!

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:12.740
Isn't it so cute?

00:00:13.160 --> 00:00:14.390
There!

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:19.160
Come on, over here!

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.000
Hurry up!

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:23.750
You went on for so long.

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:24.760
Well?

00:00:24.760 --> 00:00:26.440
Does this bathing suit look good on me?

00:00:26.440 --> 00:00:27.470
It does, right?

00:00:27.470 --> 00:00:28.960
Yup, it's nice, very nice.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:31.960
Misa-chan, you're very cute.

00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:36.590
Oh, that person! She looks like Koizumi-san!

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:38.680
Hey, why are you looking at her?

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:42.240
She's got nothing
on Koizumi-san, though.

00:00:42.240 --> 00:00:43.680
Jeez!

00:00:44.210 --> 00:00:47.810
Anyway, I didn't expect Koizumi to come,

00:00:47.810 --> 00:00:49.960
but I can't believe Jun's not here, either.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:52.440
She said she's too embarrassed 
to wear a bathing suit.

00:00:52.710 --> 00:00:56.730
Aw, man, I really wanted to see 
those two in their bathing suits.

00:00:56.730 --> 00:00:58.820
Be happy that you got to see me!

00:01:02.650 --> 00:01:05.400
I wonder what they're up to right now.

00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:10.200
Jun's probably in the library.

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:14.340
She said she's been going there every 
day since summer break started.

00:01:14.620 --> 00:01:17.340
Jun does love books.

00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:22.760
Reading over a hundred novels during 
summer break? Really?

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.960
I could never, ever do that!

00:01:24.960 --> 00:01:26.850
Yeah, huh?

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.690
Ah, I wonder what Koizumi-san is up to.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:33.110
Koizumi?

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:37.420
Well, ramen, of course, right?

00:01:38.230 --> 00:01:39.400
Yeah.

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>Penguin Home Ramen</b>

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>Ponpoko
Soy Sauce Ramen</b>

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>Avec Ramen</b>

00:01:39.990 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>Umaka-chan</b>

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.980
Koizumi-san sure does love ramen.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:45.000
<b>Risiri Kelp Ramen</b>

00:02:02.760 --> 00:02:03.470
<b>Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:02:03.470 --> 00:02:04.010
<b>Ms. Koizumi</b>

00:02:04.010 --> 00:02:04.930
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.970
<b>Local Instant Noodles</b>

00:03:19.970 --> 00:03:21.720
<b>Library</b>

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:25.970
<b>Summer Break Assignments
Literature
Mathematics B
English</b>

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:29.440
<i>This is bugging me.
I can't fully enjoy reading.</i>

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:35.500
<i>Oh, Koizumi-san.</i>

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:45.460
The school library is good for 
studying during summer break, huh?

00:03:45.460 --> 00:03:47.950
The town library tends
to be pretty busy.

00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:51.840
So is your summer report coming along?

00:03:51.840 --> 00:03:53.310
Actually, not really.

00:03:53.310 --> 00:03:54.420
You, too?

00:03:54.420 --> 00:03:58.630
I mean, yeah, talk about our future career?

00:03:58.630 --> 00:04:00.310
Our teacher just tells us to do

00:04:00.310 --> 00:04:03.680
something we like or that we're good at,
 but it's easier said than done.

00:04:03.680 --> 00:04:06.770
I don't think I could become a writer,
 and even if I were to

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:19.940
<b>Worry</b>

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:10.740
go into publishing like my mother,
 I won't necessarily end

00:04:10.740 --> 00:04:12.560
up in the department I'd like.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:15.280
Grades-wise, the natural sciences 
would be a good fit for me,

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.530
but none of the jobs associated 
with that really click with me.

00:04:18.230 --> 00:04:19.940
Not listening

00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:19.940
That's rough.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:24.760
Honestly, though, what I really 
want is to just say to heck with it,

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:28.700
and run a bookstore or be a librarian so I 
can read books all day.

00:04:29.010 --> 00:04:30.180
Yeah, right.

00:04:31.180 --> 00:04:34.080
I kind of understand that.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:45.720
Anyway, what is your dream for the future?

00:04:48.550 --> 00:04:49.720
It's a secret.

00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:51.880
I-I see.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:54.230
<i>I mean, it's something ramen-related, right?</i>

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:56.660
Anyway, I'm off now.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:58.360
Are you going somewhere after this?

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:00.460
Yes.

00:05:05.520 --> 00:05:07.700
To look at the ramen that I love.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:11.620
<b>In All 47 Prefectures of Japan
Ramen Koushien
Bar Sakura
 Osaka Yakantei Group Nerima Hikarigaoka Branch</b>

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:10.890
This place?

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.370
The sign says it's a bar.

00:05:16.190 --> 00:05:20.160
Wait, is that instant noodles?

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:22.380
<b>Hokkaido      Tohoku/Kanto      Tokai/Hokuriku</b>

00:05:20.160 --> 00:05:22.380
An entire wall of it!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:26.360
Huh? But I don't think 
I've seen many of these.

00:05:26.360 --> 00:05:27.860
You noticed, huh?

00:05:28.740 --> 00:05:32.010
The ramens they have here are 
local instant noodles from

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.640
every nook and cranny of Japan.

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:38.020
<b>Hokkaido      Tohoku/Kanto      Tokai/Hokuriku</b>

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:35.270
You're right!

00:05:35.270 --> 00:05:37.200
They're sorted by region!

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:41.540
You can get some of these 
at the supermarket chains, lately, too.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:44.530
<b>Kansai/Chuugoku       Shikoku/Kyushu      Kyushu/Okinawa</b>

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:44.530
<b>Sakura was featured in "Ikewaku."
Sakura has become a Mecca!</b>

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:44.530
I didn't know there were that 
many types of instant noodles.

00:05:45.360 --> 00:05:49.380
I often eat instant noodles
when my parents aren't home for dinner.

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:51.820
Maybe I'll take some home.

00:05:51.820 --> 00:05:53.830
I will eat them here.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.290
Huh? Here?

00:05:55.290 --> 00:05:57.830
You're going to eat instant 
noodles in the store?

00:05:58.100 --> 00:06:02.840
When I make them myself, 
I usually make a mistake.

00:06:03.170 --> 00:06:04.840
<b>Examples of failure</b>

00:06:05.080 --> 00:06:07.270
What's more, even for instant noodles,

00:06:05.880 --> 00:06:11.350
<b>The soup...</b>

00:06:06.880 --> 00:06:11.350
<b>it's become muddy</b>

00:06:07.270 --> 00:06:10.440
just one wrong step can ruin the flavor.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:14.390
Prepare the noodles and the soup separately.

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:16.100
<b><  How to Avoid  ></b>

00:06:11.350 --> 00:06:16.100
<b>Prepare the noodles and the soup separately</b>

00:06:16.270 --> 00:06:20.980
<b>The noodles...</b>

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.480
The noodles can get hard or stuck together.

00:06:17.520 --> 00:06:20.980
<b>are very hard...
 and stuck together</b>

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:24.270
Cook the noodles evenly in plenty of water.

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.610
<b>< How to Avoid ></b>

00:06:20.980 --> 00:06:25.610
<b>Cook the noodles evenly in plenty of water
 without letting them touch the air</b>

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:30.450
<b>The noodles...</b>

00:06:25.900 --> 00:06:28.950
Or the opposite. If I overcook
 the noodles, they get soggy.

00:06:26.740 --> 00:06:30.450
<b>they're soggy</b>

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:35.580
<b>< How to Avoid ></b>

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:35.580
<b>The cooking time can be ten to twenty seconds less than directed</b>

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:34.120
The cooking time can be less than directed.

00:06:35.910 --> 00:06:38.670
Oh, how many times I've suffered.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.210
<i>I guess she can't cook very well.</i>

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:46.210
Well, it's definitely a safe 
bet to have a pro make it.

00:06:47.690 --> 00:06:50.190
Maybe I'll eat here, too.

00:06:51.020 --> 00:06:55.000
So you pick something out here and have 
someone from the store cook it, right?

00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:55.760
Yes.

00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.220
Do you have any recommendations?

00:06:57.930 --> 00:07:02.240
Everyone has their own preferences, so...

00:07:02.240 --> 00:07:06.110
If I had to pick, however, I'd say 
that the products from Hokkaido are

00:07:03.440 --> 00:07:06.110
<b>Hokkaido</b>

00:07:06.110 --> 00:07:09.700
<b>Sapporo Ramen Shirakanba Retreats</b>

00:07:06.280 --> 00:07:11.200
<b>Sapporo Junren</b>

00:07:06.470 --> 00:07:09.210
all a cut above the rest.

00:07:08.030 --> 00:07:11.610
<b>Soy Sauce Ramen</b>

00:07:09.210 --> 00:07:11.610
They have many collaborations 
with famous restaurants, too.

00:07:09.320 --> 00:07:11.610
<b>Butaking</b>

00:07:11.610 --> 00:07:14.830
And beginning with the Maruyama Zoo Ramen,
 the ramens associated with

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:19.750
each region's zoos have cute packaging,
but also take their taste seriously, too.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:25.050
Another animal-associated type would be 
Aichi's Nishimikawa Giraffe Ramen series.

00:07:19.750 --> 00:07:25.210
<b>Giraffe Home Ramen</b>

00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:28.510
<b>Penguin Home Ramen</b>

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:31.380
<b>Seal Home ramen</b>

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:29.760
Yet another would be the Aquarium 
series, such as Penguin, Dolphin, and Seal.

00:07:25.750 --> 00:07:33.550
<b>Dolphin Home Ramen</b>

00:07:29.760 --> 00:07:32.680
They also have a healthier variant with 
non-fried noodles, called the beauty series.

00:07:30.010 --> 00:07:37.810
<b>Beauty Women's Ramen</b>

00:07:32.680 --> 00:07:35.710
Then there is the Higashimikawa 
region's Ponpoko Ramen.

00:07:34.010 --> 00:07:38.270
<b>Ponpoko Soy Sauce Ramen</b>

00:07:35.710 --> 00:07:38.270
Both have a gentle,
 homemade flavor.

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:43.430
The nonstandard types include various 
ingredients in the noodles, such as

00:07:38.270 --> 00:07:43.440
Olive Ramen

00:07:39.770 --> 00:07:46.150
<b>Lotus Root Ramen</b>

00:07:41.690 --> 00:07:46.150
<b>Cayenne Pepper Miso Ramen</b>

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:46.150
<b>Risiri Kelp Ramen</b>

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:46.150
olive, lotus root, chili, or kelp, allowing you to experience unique flavors.

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:52.280
<b>Champon Ramen</b>

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:54.320
<b>Umaka-chan
Mustard Ramen</b>

00:07:46.490 --> 00:07:50.440
Additionally, there are these Chanpon ramen 
from Hyogo, which are close to salt tanmen.

00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:56.200
<b>Umaka-chan</b>

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:54.090
Beware, though, they are quite different 
from Kyushu's Nagasaki chanpon.

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:59.410
<b>Umaka-chan
Kumamoto-style
Tonkotsu</b>

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:59.410
<b>Umaka-chan
Kurume-style
Tonkotsu</b>

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:59.410
<b>Umaka-chan
Kurobuta Tonkotsu</b>

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:56.160
For some reason, they're very
 popular in Ishikawa.

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.410
Speaking of Kyushu, notable are the 
tonkotsu-flavored Umakacchan series,

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:04.150
and the Avec Ramen from Kumamoto,
 which comes with a light salt soup paste.

00:07:59.410 --> 00:08:06.840
<b>Avec Ramen</b>

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:07.920
<b>Maru-chan
Double Ramen</b>

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:07.130
They call it "Avec" because 
it has two servings, apparently.

00:08:07.130 --> 00:08:10.240
In Hokkaido, the Double Ramen
 is something similar.

00:08:11.480 --> 00:08:12.690
<i>So much...</i>

00:08:12.690 --> 00:08:15.820
<i>Wait a minute, why does 
she already know every flavor?</i>

00:08:15.820 --> 00:08:17.680
<i>Does this mean she's tried every single one?</i>

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:21.300
<i>If she's doing this much research, 
does it mean that she's pursuing</i>

00:08:22.790 --> 00:08:26.050
<i>a career in the ramen industry?!</i>

00:08:29.290 --> 00:08:33.950
So anyway, I went for the 
Hokkaido Rishiri Kelp Ramen.

00:08:34.270 --> 00:08:38.490
I picked Ichiki Kushino Specialty Tuna Ramen
 from Kagoshima Prefecture,

00:08:38.490 --> 00:08:40.450
with powdered wasabi.

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:43.730
These look like they came
 from a real ramen restaurant.

00:08:43.730 --> 00:08:44.460
Well...

00:08:45.380 --> 00:08:47.080
Time to eat.

00:09:00.450 --> 00:09:02.720
<i>There's a stronger kelp flavor
 than I expected.</i>

00:09:03.230 --> 00:09:07.020
<i>The umami of the shredded kelp 
is spreading more and more.</i>

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:08.980
<i>Huh?</i>

00:09:09.750 --> 00:09:10.630
<i>Huh?!</i>

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.990
<b>Risiri Island, Hokkaido</b>

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.990
<b>Risiri Kelp Ramen</b>

00:09:12.990 --> 00:09:15.990
<b>Noodles with Risiri kelp
and a light soup that complements
its flavor.</b>

00:09:23.160 --> 00:09:28.260
<i>I don't remember instant noodles
ever being this good.</i>

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.080
The powdered wasabi got in my nose.

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.890
But that's the fun part.

00:09:41.960 --> 00:09:48.150
Koizumi-san, you're going to have 
a career in the ramen industry, right?

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:51.840
That's why you're always going around, 
training your sense of taste

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:55.760
and deepening your
 understanding of ramen, right?

00:09:55.760 --> 00:09:58.660
I sort of look up to you for that.

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:01.080
Huh?

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:01.580
Huh?

00:10:01.660 --> 00:10:02.080
Huh?

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:02.950
Huh?

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.620
I never really thought about that.

00:10:06.620 --> 00:10:08.170
I-I see.

00:10:16.610 --> 00:10:23.410
In fact, I can't even 
think about anything...

00:10:23.410 --> 00:10:26.200
when I'm eating ramen.

00:10:30.360 --> 00:10:34.180
I kind of know what you mean.

00:10:36.360 --> 00:10:37.820
You're right.

00:10:38.260 --> 00:10:41.200
This is this, that is that.

00:10:41.200 --> 00:10:42.020
Right.

00:10:43.390 --> 00:10:46.580
So what is your dream for the future?

00:10:50.650 --> 00:10:51.960
It's a secret.

00:10:52.960 --> 00:10:56.200
What do I have to do
to become ramen?

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:57.840
What are you talking about?

00:10:59.170 --> 00:10:59.880
<b>Sniff</b>

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.260
Sniff, sniff...

00:10:59.590 --> 00:11:00.300
<b>Sniff</b>

00:11:00.590 --> 00:11:01.300
<b>Sniff</b>

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:01.720
Sniff, sniff...

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:01.680
<b>Sniff</b>

00:11:02.250 --> 00:11:07.680
The instant noodles you gave me
 kind of smell like Koizumi-san.

00:11:07.680 --> 00:11:08.540
What?!

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.940
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:11:15.400 --> 00:11:19.320
<b>Iekei</b>

00:11:21.870 --> 00:11:24.320
The egg topping will be 70 yen.

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:26.730
Thank you for waiting!

00:11:26.730 --> 00:11:28.330
Thank you for waiting!

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:31.260
Next customer, please!

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:32.500
Welcome!

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:34.130
Welcome!

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:38.130
The spicy miso cabbage is 120 yen!

00:11:39.420 --> 00:11:40.880
Thank you for waiting!

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.510
Thank you for waiting!

00:12:13.990 --> 00:12:16.000
Hey, what do you want to have for lunch?

00:12:16.490 --> 00:12:17.970
I want ramen.

00:12:17.970 --> 00:12:18.780
Rice.

00:12:18.780 --> 00:12:19.800
A rice dish.

00:12:19.800 --> 00:12:21.010
Noodles or something.

00:12:21.650 --> 00:12:27.220
How about you guys put your rice
in our ramen soup after we're done?

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:29.500
I guess that's a thing.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:31.480
I'm fine with ramen, then.

00:12:31.480 --> 00:12:32.100
What?

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:35.080
Putting rice into ramen broth?

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.480
Isn't that kinda gross?

00:12:37.650 --> 00:12:39.390
Are you being serious right now?!

00:12:39.390 --> 00:12:42.680
The soup's heavenly richness makes
finishing it with rice a no-brainer!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:44.490
I've never done such a thing.

00:12:44.490 --> 00:12:45.720
Besides, I prefer light flavors.

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:47.440
Now, now...

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:49.880
I used to be a denier just 
like you until recently.

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:51.770
Leftover broth and rice?

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:54.470
If you want rice so badly, 
just get a small fried rice.

00:12:54.470 --> 00:12:56.660
If you want more volume, 
just order more noodles.

00:12:56.660 --> 00:12:57.750
You know?

00:12:58.040 --> 00:12:58.650
But...

00:12:58.650 --> 00:13:02.210
The other day, I went to a ramen shop with 
my girlfriend and the cook recommended it,

00:13:02.210 --> 00:13:04.290
so I tried it for the first time.

00:13:04.290 --> 00:13:06.790
Result? Total satisfaction.

00:13:06.790 --> 00:13:11.850
My girlfriend was totally happy, too, saying, 
"Delicious! It's like an Italian risotto!"

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:14.690
By now, I'm fully converted.

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:17.250
Nobody asked you to brag 
about having a girlfriend.

00:13:17.250 --> 00:13:19.770
Come on, I sided with you!

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:24.150
Vegetable potage types 
<i>do</i> work well rice.

00:13:24.610 --> 00:13:26.720
And seafood types.

00:13:26.720 --> 00:13:28.870
Katsuura tantan works really well, too.

00:13:28.870 --> 00:13:31.410
Yes, and add an egg on top!

00:13:31.830 --> 00:13:34.940
Then why not just order 
porridge from the get-go?

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:36.720
You don't get it.

00:13:36.720 --> 00:13:39.170
It's good because you're finishing
it with rice <i>after</i> the ramen!

00:13:39.610 --> 00:13:43.120
Rice with ramen is carbs on carbs.

00:13:43.120 --> 00:13:48.050
When you eat rice and ramen together, 
the ramen functions as the side dish and the soup!

00:13:48.560 --> 00:13:51.760
But for being a soup, doesn't it 
have too much stuff in it?

00:13:51.760 --> 00:13:53.650
Come on!

00:13:53.650 --> 00:13:57.490
I'm fine with ramen, but can
 we please pick a place?

00:13:57.490 --> 00:13:59.200
I'm hungry.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:00.270
Yeah, sorry.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.110
Let's see...

00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:07.650
Which shop has the ramen
that goes best with rice?

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:11.910
<b>The customer
is the master
of our flavor</b>

00:14:07.650 --> 00:14:11.910
<b>Iekei Birthplace Yoshimuraya
 Head Chef: Yoshimura Minoru</b>

00:14:10.760 --> 00:14:11.910
Household?

00:14:12.350 --> 00:14:14.690
Does that mean it'll taste
like it's homemade?

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:17.660
No, this is "iekei."

00:14:17.660 --> 00:14:23.990
Like, it has spinach and nori on it, and it's rich.
It's like tonkotsu, but it's also like chicken.

00:14:23.990 --> 00:14:25.420
Anyway, it's just delicious!

00:14:25.850 --> 00:14:27.940
That failed to explain it.

00:14:26.440 --> 00:14:28.840
Man, the lineup is super long again.

00:14:27.940 --> 00:14:33.400
Shut up! Anyway, iekei is the 
perfect companion for rice!

00:14:33.400 --> 00:14:38.520
Iekei is something that began here,
 at this Yoshimuraya.

00:14:38.520 --> 00:14:43.460
Almost all the restaurants that have their roots here
have the kanji "ie" or "ya" in their names,

00:14:43.460 --> 00:14:45.940
so they got grouped together
under the "iekei" label.

00:14:46.400 --> 00:14:48.440
Though the definition is not really solid.

00:14:48.440 --> 00:14:49.320
That's it!

00:14:49.320 --> 00:14:52.970
Oh yeah, it's true.
 There are quite a lot of them.

00:14:52.970 --> 00:14:54.950
Let's get in line already.

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.700
<b>Iekei Birthplace       Ramen Yoshimuraya</b>

00:14:54.950 --> 00:14:57.700
All right, let's go!

00:14:59.100 --> 00:15:01.130
Thanks for waiting.

00:15:02.310 --> 00:15:04.550
I can't take it, it looks so good!

00:15:04.550 --> 00:15:06.270
I have to send this to my girlfriend.

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:09.550
Huh? You're on social media?

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:10.970
Let's eat.

00:15:09.550 --> 00:15:10.970
No, it's just for my records.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:14.770
Hey, isn't this too much?
 I don't know if I can finish it.

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:17.470
Who cares! Let's just eat.

00:15:17.970 --> 00:15:19.600
Time to eat!

00:15:29.450 --> 00:15:30.440
A stable flavor.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.330
It has a hint of game, but it's 
creamy and goes down easily.

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.870
It's so good that you'll die if you
 can't eat it regularly!

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:39.770
Yeah, this is actually really delicious.

00:15:39.770 --> 00:15:40.500
See?!

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:44.650
Would you like some garlic? 
Or do you prefer ginger?

00:15:44.650 --> 00:15:46.010
Saburou?

00:15:46.010 --> 00:15:48.580
After this, I have to go to work, 
where I to talk to people.

00:15:48.580 --> 00:15:49.880
I'll stick with ginger.

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:53.430
I'll take garlic. I'm going home after this.

00:15:53.430 --> 00:15:56.600
I'm jealous. I have to go to work, too.

00:15:56.600 --> 00:16:00.790
Oh, hey, when do you guys eat your spinach?

00:16:00.790 --> 00:16:02.000
I eat it at the beginning.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:03.730
If you ask me, I'd say at the end.

00:16:03.730 --> 00:16:05.720
I've never even thought about that.

00:16:05.720 --> 00:16:07.770
I eat it with my rice.

00:16:08.130 --> 00:16:10.070
Then what about the nori? 
When do you eat that?

00:16:11.250 --> 00:16:14.450
I mean, I never got why there's nori on ramen.

00:16:15.030 --> 00:16:19.070
It's not clear when you should eat it, 
and if you leave it, it just gets soggy.

00:16:19.070 --> 00:16:20.950
That's what's good about it!

00:16:21.330 --> 00:16:26.790
See, you wrap the spinach in 
the soup-soaked nori like this.

00:16:27.830 --> 00:16:29.800
This is the stuff!

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:35.800
So good!

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:40.580
The nori on ramen can only really 
shine fully when there's rice.

00:16:40.580 --> 00:16:42.380
So true.

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:47.060
This is good.

00:16:47.600 --> 00:16:50.320
Just eating it with 
the noodles is good, too.

00:16:50.890 --> 00:16:54.320
If you let the nori soak up the soup,
and eat it with the noodles, you can

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:57.940
enjoy both the noodles and 
the soup at the same time.

00:16:59.380 --> 00:17:04.290
Yeah. Both ways are good, but now
 I feel like there's not enough nori.

00:17:04.580 --> 00:17:08.120
If that's the case,
 you can just order extra nori.

00:17:08.120 --> 00:17:09.210
I see.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.170
Alternatively... Bam!

00:17:12.770 --> 00:17:14.670
That's the ticket.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:16.250
This looks so good.

00:17:16.250 --> 00:17:20.740
<i>It does look good, but then you 
end up drinking all of the soup.</i>

00:17:21.560 --> 00:17:22.680
<i>The sodium...</i>

00:17:23.150 --> 00:17:25.320
Hey guys, what's your stance 
on vinegar in ramen?

00:17:25.320 --> 00:17:26.440
Yay or nay?

00:17:26.700 --> 00:17:29.930
I like to add it at the end
to change up the flavor.

00:17:29.930 --> 00:17:32.190
Welcome.

00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.160
Oh, a high school girl!

00:17:43.530 --> 00:17:45.660
Don't stare like that.

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.530
Hm? I feel like I've seen her before.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:52.300
How thick would you like your soup?

00:17:53.640 --> 00:17:58.300
Thicker soup, less fat, 
and the noodles a bit firm.

00:18:00.980 --> 00:18:01.900
<i>Sodium...</i>

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:04.680
Here you go, ramen and rice!

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:06.500
Thank you for waiting.

00:18:08.240 --> 00:18:09.560
Time to eat.

00:18:38.390 --> 00:18:41.020
<i>She kind of created a new dish!</i>

00:18:41.020 --> 00:18:44.640
I see, putting soup into 
your rice bowl works, too.

00:19:08.390 --> 00:19:10.040
<i>She's a master!</i>

00:19:10.040 --> 00:19:14.750
I see, she ordered her noodles firm 
because she eats her rice first.

00:19:44.200 --> 00:19:46.030
Thank you for the meal!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:54.220
I think you're right.
Iekei ramen goes well with rice.

00:19:54.220 --> 00:19:55.540
See?!

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:58.660
Iekei is the best!

00:20:06.130 --> 00:20:10.310
Chopped ginger and grated ginger are usually 
both available, which is helpful.

00:20:11.310 --> 00:20:14.000
At this place I was at the other day, 
I put chopped onion on and it was way

00:20:14.000 --> 00:20:16.060
more refreshing than I had imagined.

00:20:16.060 --> 00:20:20.790
That's why I think free toppings are a 
crucial element to truly enjoying iekei ramen,

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:21.980
so much that...

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:23.900
<i>He's become a complete fanboy.</i>

00:20:25.230 --> 00:20:27.750
Which ramen shop are you going to today?

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:29.560
Lately, there's been an iekei boom.

00:20:29.560 --> 00:20:32.960
Huh? What's that?
Does it taste like it's homemade?

00:20:32.960 --> 00:20:34.200
Then just come over to my place!

00:20:34.200 --> 00:20:34.960
I will not.

00:20:37.460 --> 00:20:39.960
<b>Ms. Koizumi
Loves Ramen
Noodles</b>

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:29.950
<b>Mountain</b>

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:29.950
<b>Pork Guy</b>

00:22:09.930 --> 00:22:29.950
<b>Back Fat</b>

00:22:11.720 --> 00:22:14.930
Cabbage as a topping has a rep for 
diluting the soup, but I like it because

00:22:14.930 --> 00:22:16.600
it makes the flavor a bit more rounded.

00:22:16.600 --> 00:22:19.680
Seriously? You noticing that 
means you've made real progress!

00:22:19.680 --> 00:22:21.900
I sometimes put nattou on as a topping.

00:22:21.900 --> 00:22:25.320
I've heard that vanilla ice cream on
 soy sauce, potato salad on tonkotsu, and

00:22:25.320 --> 00:22:27.350
honey on miso are viable, too.

00:22:27.350 --> 00:22:29.950
That's too sophisticated
for me to even imagine.

00:22:29.950 --> 00:22:35.950
<b>Thank you for the food!</b>
